        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.337,
            0.847,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": "**Prism:** A prism, in general, has two congruent polygons as opposite faces, with edges connecting the corresponding vertices of these polygons. All the other faces are parallelograms. Based on the shape of the congruent polygons, prisms may be called triangular prisms, pentagonal prisms, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.429,
            0.847,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "**Pyramids:** A pyramid, in general, has a polygonal base and a point outside it, and edges connect the point with each of the vertices of the base. Based on the shape of the base, pyramids may be called triangular pyramids, square pyramids, pentagonal pyramids, and so on. A triangular pyramid is also known as a **tetrahedron**."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.53,
            0.376,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
