        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.7,
            0.847,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "？ If the congruent polygons of a prism have 10 sides, how many faces, edges and vertices does the prism have? What if the polygons have n sides?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.773,
            0.846,
            0.814
          ],
          "content": "？ If the base of a pyramid has 10 sides, how many faces, edges and vertices does the pyramid have? What if the base is an n-sided polygon?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.822,
            0.846,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": "Now we will see how to make different solids using a foldable flat surface such as paper, cardboard, etc."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.859,
            0.847,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": "The basic idea is to create a shape on a flat surface that can be folded into the solid. Such a shape is called a **net**. In other words, a net is obtained by ‘unfolding’ a solid onto a plane."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
